   of simdgroup_matrix<T,8,8>. Represent as MSL struct: `struct spvCoopmat_<T> { simdgroup_matrix<T,8,8> t[4]; }`
   (t[0]=TL,t[1]=TR,t[2]=BL,t[3]=BR). Emit the struct defs once (like spirv-cross emits other helper types).
 STEP 2a: CompilerMSL::type_to_glsl (spirv_msl.cpp:16493 switch on type.basetype) — add case for the coop
   matrix type (SPIRType for OpTypeCooperativeMatrixKHR) → return the spvCoopmat_<elem> struct name; register
   the helper struct for emission. (GLSL base emits `coopmat<...>` at spirv_glsl.cpp:16937 — do NOT inherit.)
 STEP 2b: CompilerMSL::emit_instruction (spirv_msl.cpp:9361) — add cases:
   - OpCooperativeMatrixLoadKHR: for tile (r,c) in 2x2: simdgroup_load(res.t[r*2+c], ptr + (r*8*stride + c*8),
     stride, /*transpose per RowMajor/ColMajor*/). ptr is the vector<4xf32> workgroup buffer reinterpreted;
     use the byte offset from the access-chain + the runtime stride operand.
   - OpCooperativeMatrixStoreKHR: inverse (simdgroup_store per tile).
   - OpCooperativeMatrixMulAddKHR (C = A*B + C, A=MxK B=KxN C=MxN, all 16 → 2x2 tiles): triple loop
     for i in 0..1, j in 0..1: acc=C.t[i*2+j]; for k in 0..1: simdgroup_multiply_accumulate(acc, A.t[i*2+k],
     B.t[k*2+j], acc); res.t[i*2+j]=acc.
