2026-07-13 (cont26): MAJOR DIAGNOSTIC BREAKTHROUGH — pinpointed the GQA NaN to the DISPATCH using the now-working iree-run-module + --iree-flow-trace-dispatch-tensors. Built a minimal 4-input repro (/tmp/minscore.py: emb,ids,wq,wk -> rms(gather) -> q/k proj -> GQA -> scores; NaN confirmed) + saved inputs as .npy. Traced on metal: the FIRST bad output is main_dispatch_7_matmul_1024x128x512_bf16xbf16xf32 = the K-PROJECTION matmul (k=mm(rms(gather),wk), N=KV*dh=128). Its INPUTS are FINITE (h=[0.03,2.04,...], wk=[-0.003,0.01,...]) but its OUTPUT is GARBAGE (-4.8E+09, 3.4E-24, 3.4E+38, denormals) -> an in-context matmul codegen MISCOMPILE (not a NaN-propagation; the matmul itself produces garbage). q-projection (dispatch_4, 1024x512x512, N=512) is FINITE. Isolated 1024x128x512 (random inputs) is FINITE for all N incl 128 -> so it's CONTEXT-dependent (the specific fused input layout from rms(gather) + N=128 + the [1024,128]->[B,T,KV,dh] reshape/transpose consumer). Keeping k in f32 (late bf16 cast) still NaN -> not purely the bf16 store-downcast. So: a coop matmul codegen miscompile for the N=128 projection fed by rms(gather) and consumed by a KV-head reshape+GQA-repeat. Deployed + hero UNTOUCHED. NEXT: isolate the exact trigger — build a standalone MLIR of [dispatch_7 in-context] (h from rms(gather) + N=128 + reshape consumer) and bisect which factor (input memref layout / N=128 coop tiling / reshape-fused-store) makes the coop matmul emit garbage; then fix the coop codegen or gate that shape off coop.
2026-07-13 (cont27): Sharpened the GQA-NaN root cause. CONFIRMED: the miscompiling dispatch_7 (k-proj 1024x128x512) IS on the COOP path (NLEARN_COOP_DEBUG: N=128 COOP), and q-proj (N=512) is also COOP but FINITE. Tested tile configs SG{1,2,4}xMNT{1,2,4} on the minimal repro -> ALL NaN, so it's CONFIG-INDEPENDENT. Combined with: isolated 1024x128x512 (random inputs) is FINITE. => It's a CONTEXT-TRIGGERED coop matmul codegen miscompile: the coop matmul emits GARBAGE (finite in -> -4.8E+09/3.4E+38/denormals out) specifically when fed by rms(gather) AND consumed by the [1024,128]->[B,T,KV,dh] KV-head reshape/transpose (GQA), independent of tile config and not reproduced by the shape alone. This is the precise dispatch-level root cause of the GQA (llama-3/mistral) NaN — a big step from 'mysterious combination NaN'. Enabled by the iree-run-module + --iree-flow-trace-dispatch-tensors tooling built cont25. Deployed + hero UNTOUCHED. NEXT: dump dispatch_7's generated SPIR-V/MSL (iree-compile --mlir-print-ir-after / dump-executable-sources for that one dispatch) and inspect the coop store/load codegen to find why the fused rms-input + KV-reshape context makes it emit garbage; then fix the coop codegen or precisely gate that fusion context off coop. Shape-based gating is WRONG (isolated N=128 is fine) — must gate/fix by the fusion context.
