2026-07-13 (cont29): EXACT root cause of the GQA NaN nailed at the SPIR-V level (extracted raw MSL+SPIR-V via iree-hal-dump-executable-intermediates-to + strings on the metallib=false vmfb). d7 (broken k-proj N=128) vs d4 (working q-proj N=512): d7 = `CooperativeMatrixStore coopmatrix<16x16xBF16,MatrixAcc>, stride=16`; d4 = `CooperativeMatrixStore coopmatrix<16x16xF32,MatrixAcc>, stride=128`. => the k-proj coop matmul gets a BF16 ACCUMULATOR, which is INVALID on the Apple target (its MMA intrinsics WMMAR4_F32 / NV_WMMA_F32 are f32-accumulate-ONLY, no bf16-acc) -> garbage output from finite inputs. The truncf(bf16) fused into the coop store making a bf16-acc store for the N=128 k-proj, while the N=512 q-proj kept f32-acc + separate truncf. RULED OUT every knob (all still NaN): tile configs SG/MNT, NO_CPROMOTE, NO_WAR, BARRIER, early-trunc-fusion off, transpose-propagation off, UPCAST_ACC on. => needs a SOURCE fix in the coop-store lowering: force f32-accumulator store (prevent the bf16 truncf fusing into the coop store) for matmuls whose bf16 truncf would otherwise create an invalid bf16-acc store. Reverted the early-trunc env gate. NO REGRESSION (gpt2 ~3.4). Deployed + hero UNTOUCHED. NEXT: find in the SPIRV coop codegen where the k-proj store becomes bf16-acc (VectorToGPU subgroup_mma_elementwise truncf before store, or SPIRVTileAndPromote C-store) and force f32-acc store there for this pattern; validate minscore/cov_probe finite + gpt2/llama no-regression.
