2026-07-13 (cont35): GQA root cause localized to the EXACT Milestone-2 code (spirv_cross/spirv_msl.cpp). Mechanism: OpFConvert for a coop matrix (line ~9480) ALIASES the convert result to the source expression via emit_op(expression_type_id(ops[2])...). This is correct for WIDENING input converts (bf16->f32 A/B for mixed-precision simdgroup_multiply_accumulate) but WRONG for the NARROWING C-accumulator truncf(f32->bf16) before a store: the store (OpCooperativeMatrixStore, line ~9447) then uses the aliased matrix element type (f32) -> reinterpret_cast<device float*> -> stores the f32 accumulator matrix (4 bytes/elem) into the bf16 output buffer (2 bytes/elem) -> GARBAGE (the observed simdgroup_store device-float* stride-16 in d7). q-proj is C-promoted by IREE (f32 staging + separate truncf, no coop OpFConvert store) so it's fine. FIX (path c, intricate + uncertain): make the narrowing coop store convert f32->bf16 (emit eptr as bfloat* with bf16 stride IF Metal simdgroup_store converts across element types; else materialize the narrowing) — needs Metal simdgroup_store cross-type semantics verified. STOPPING GQA definitively (14 turns across config/VectorToGPU/fallback/spirv_cross = same bug, spinning). COMPLETE diagnosis at exact code lines logged for a focused spirv_cross fix. Deployed + hero UNTOUCHED. Fork validated 88-91% inf / 67% train of jax-metal, matrix units, broad coverage. All 3 levers fully-diagnosed hard blockers.
2026-07-13 (cont36): DEFINITIVELY ELIMINATED GQA fix path (c) by experiment. Modified spirv_cross OpFConvert to register the TRUE bf16 result type for narrowing coop converts -> the store correctly emitted `reinterpret_cast<device bfloat*>` with the right bf16 stride (16u*8=128) BUT the MSL FAILS TO COMPILE: Metal's `simdgroup_store(simdgroup_matrix<T,C,R>, device T*, ...)` REQUIRES the matrix element type T to MATCH the pointer type — no cross-type store. So storing an f32 simdgroup_matrix (the aliased C accumulator) through bfloat* is a template mismatch. Metal has NO simdgroup element conversion primitive, so a coop f32->bf16 store CANNOT be expressed at the Metal/spirv_cross level. => path (c) [spirv_msl.cpp fix] is IMPOSSIBLE; the GQA fix is UNIQUELY path (b): IREE-side C-promotion (stage the f32 accumulator to memory, then a separate scalar/vector truncf to bf16 — exactly what the working q-proj does). Reverted the spirv_cross change (added a NOTE documenting why); gpt2 3.49 no-regression. NEXT (path b, the only remaining GQA fix): investigate why SPIRVTileAndPromote does NOT stage the k-proj C matrix despite needToPromote=true — dump the SPIR-V with the needToPromote-force-truncf fix re-added and check for a workgroup C buffer / f32 store vs the direct bf16 store; if staging still doesn't happen, the C-promotion gating in SPIRVTileAndPromote (promoteCMatrix flag path) needs the fix. Deployed + hero UNTOUCHED. Fork validated 88-91% inf / 67% train of jax-metal.
2026-07-13 (cont37): ✅✅ GQA NaN FIXED — VALIDATED MILESTONE (16 turns of diagnosis paid off). ROOT CAUSE (final): SPIRVTileAndPromote::doPromoteCMatrix's op-collection filter (line ~326) SKIPS all single-input f32->bf16 generics as "input-trunc PROLOGUE" producers — but this ALSO wrongly skipped the EPILOGUE store-downcast truncf (same signature), leaving linalgOps=[matmul] -> size<=1 -> early return -> NO C-promotion -> the invalid bf16 coop store of the f32 accumulator -> GARBAGE (the GQA k-proj N=128). FIX: find the matmul (reduction op), and only skip the f32->bf16 generic if it's a PROLOGUE (its input is NOT the matmul output); KEEP the EPILOGUE (input == matmul output base buffer) so C gets promoted (f32 staging + separate truncf = the correct path the working q-proj already takes). Scoped to small-N (matmul out N<=256) to avoid force-promoting large FFN/proj matmuls (that forward-fuse their truncf) — recovered most of an ~11% training regression (unscoped 1.65 -> scoped ~1.7-1.79 vs baseline 1.86). RESULT: minscore finite, cov_probe CORRECT (0.360797 vs CPU 0.360737), llama grad still EXACT (w1 15.95=CPU); modern GQA LLMs (llama-3/mistral: gather+GQA+tied-LM-head) went from GARBAGE -> CORRECT. NO INFERENCE REGRESSION (gpt2 3.44, bert 2.89, vit 0.65, llama 2.23 — noise); small training cost (~5-8% from small-N backward matmuls now C-promoted). Default-on (opt-out NLEARN_COOP_NO_PROMOTE_DOWNCAST). Deployed + hero UNTOUCHED (all via IREE_PJRT_COMPILER_LIB_PATH). Enabled by the iree-run-module dispatch-trace + raw MSL/SPIR-V extraction tooling built cont25-29. NEXT: tighten the N-scope or detect the exact invalid-store pattern to zero out the training cost; then the remaining levers are flash-attn + MPS-kernel-quality.
