2026-07-13 (cont40): CLOSED the isolated-matmul / MPS-parity-kernel lever BY MEASUREMENT (was a vague "88% ceiling"). Dumped the isolated bf16 FFN coop matmul MSL (4096x768x3072, iree-hal-dump-executable-intermediates + strings on metallib=false vmfb): inner K-loop is SINGLE-BUFFERED — per K-iter does barrier -> copy global->threadgroup -> barrier -> 32 simdgroup_load + 64 simdgroup_multiply_accumulate. Hypothesized the missing double-buffering (2 barriers/iter, no global/compute overlap) was the ~2x gap vs MPS's pipelined GEMM. FALSIFIED by A/B: NLEARN_COOP_PD/SS DOES change codegen (PD=2 -> multibuf'd prologue/epilogue, 6 barriers, 3x ops) but throughput does NOT improve: PD=0 baseline 2.97 TFLOP/s vs PD=1_SS1 2.82 vs PD=1_SS0 2.78 (pipelining marginally SLOWER). Root cause of the earlier "flat PD sweep" now mechanistic: (a) AppleConfig.cpp:93 defaults softwarePipelineDepth=0 AND the coop path (KernelConfig.cpp:1099) has NO default-to-1 (unlike scalar path :731) so coop is single-buffered by default; (b) with the real bf16 truncf epilogue (C-promotion, promoteC=1) PD>=2 OVERFLOWS threadgroup mem (40960>32768) -> errors/refused -> silently stays single-buffered; (c) the coop matmul is COMPUTE-BOUND on the matrix units + 4-subgroup occupancy hides the copy latency, so single-buffering is fine. => isolated-matmul kernel quality is NOT the lever. ALSO: jax-metal 0.4.34 now CRASHES on this box (macOS 26) for both bf16 AND f32 matmul (MetalClient destroyed, no output) -> the "88% of jax-metal" ceiling is STALE; the fork is currently the ONLY working bf16 backend. Full-forward rates confirm matmul path is healthy: gpt2-small fwd 3.37 TFLOP/s, gpt2 fwd 2.62 (>= isolated 2.97), so attention/glue doesn't drag the forward. => residual training-MFU gap to MLX (deep-24L 2.35) is NOT isolated-matmul kernel quality nor fwd attention overhead; it's the BACKWARD pass / deep-graph behavior. Only substantive remaining throughput lever = flash-attn (deep LLVMGPU-vector-distribute por