2026-07-13 (cont41): FULLY LOCALIZED the training-MFU gap to ATTENTION by measurement (decisive). gpt2 fwd 2.62 vs fwd+bwd 0.94 TFLOP/s -> backward-only ~0.71 (3.7x slower/FLOP). But the backward GEMMs are NOT the cause: (1) transposed backward matmuls dW=x^T@dy [768x3072x4096] and dx=dy@w^T [4096x768x3072] BOTH hit coop (64 MACs) and run at 3.36 TFLOP/s isolated (>= fwd 3.05) — old "transposed backward -> scalar" suspicion FALSIFIED; (2) A/B on bench.py copy with NO_ATTN toggle: gpt2 fwd+bwd WITH attn 3235ms/0.95 TFLOP/s vs NO attn 1194ms/2.56 TFLOP/s => ATTENTION IS 63% OF THE STEP (2041ms) and is the SOLE source of the MFU collapse; the non-attention path (all FFN/proj GEMMs fwd+bwd + glue) runs at 2.56 = healthy, == forward. (3) The attention batch-matmuls q@k^T [1024x1024x64] and a@v [1024x64x1024] BOTH hit coop too (64 MACs) — so attention slowness is NOT scalar matmuls; it's the materialized T×T score matrix (gpt2: [48,1024,1024]=~200MB) round-tripped through ~10 memory-bound elementwise dispatches (scale/causal-mask/softmax max-exp-sum-div) + q/k/v transposes, DOUBLED in backward (+ softmax-bwd/dScores). => CONFIRMS flash-attention (avoid T×T materialization, online softmax, few fused dispatches) as THE lever for the generalized-backend goal, and explains why the whole coop-matmul campaign never moved training MFU (matmuls were never the bottleneck — all coop + fast). Deployed + hero UNTOUCHED (Jul 13 06:16); all measurement via IREE_PJRT_COMPILER_LIB_PATH override + read-only dumps. NEXT: attack attention. Concrete first step = check whether jax.nn.dot_product_attention lowers to iree_linalg_ext.attention and whether the DORMANT scaffolded SPIRVVectorDistributeAttention pipeline (opt-in NLEARN_COOP_ATTENTION_WIP) can compile it with per-op decompositionConfig (qk/pv lowering_configs) added to setAttentionOpConfig -> the missing piece from cont22-23 that made it hang on un-tiled scores.
2026-07-13 (cont42): ✅ VALIDATED COVERAGE MILESTONE — jax.nn.dot_product_attention now compiles+runs correct on the fork (was a hard compile crash). Root cause (found while starting the flash-attn build): jax.nn.dot_product_attention decomposes to explicit dot_general+softmax (NOT a fused attention op — IREE's iree-stablehlo-convert-flash-attention-dispatch pass does NOT fire on metal; jax only emits the fused custom_call on CUDA/cuDNN), and the attention dot_generals carry a #stablehlo.dot_algorithm attr (bf16xbf16->f32-accum) which upstream stablehlo-legalize-to-linalg marks ILLEGAL -> whole-module fail ("failed to legalize operation 'stablehlo.dot_general'"). Minimal 3-line repro (/tmp/da_min.mlir) confirmed isolable. FIX: added a preprocessing pattern DropDotAlgorithm in compiler/plugins/input/StableHLO/Conversion/Preprocessing/StableHLOToStableHLO.cpp (strips the algorithm attr from dot_general, benefit=500 so it runs before dot lowering; semantics-preserving since element types already encode bf16-in/f32-accum = the coop path). Rebuilt standalone iree-compile (6s incremental). VALIDATED: da_min compiles w/ 64 coop MACs; full jax.nn.dot_product_attention (B2 H4 T256 dh64, causal, bf16) rel_err=0.0048 vs numpy CPU ref (<5e-2 PASS); NO regression (gpt2-small 3.38 TFLOP/s unchanged). NOT deployed (hero doesn't use this API; conservative — fix preserved in tree for next bundled deploy). Deployed compiler + hero UNTOUCHED (Jul 13 06:16). NOTE: this is a COVERAGE win (modern jax attention API runs), NOT a speed win — the attention still decomposes to memory-bound T×T ops (the 63% MFU sink from cont41 stands). NEXT: for SPEED, the fused-attention path needs (a) pattern-recognition to FORM iree_linalg_ext.attention from the decomposed dot_general+softmax (since iree-stablehlo-convert-flash-attention-dispatch only fires on the CUDA custom_call, not metal's decomposed form) THEN (b) the SPIRV attention codegen (scaffold hangs on un-tiled scores). Investigate whether IREE