2026-07-16 cont304: ✅ LANDED regression-free bf16-prologue-fusion COMPILE fix (VectorToGPU.cpp elementwiseSupportsMMAMatrixType). Root: SPIR-V coop-matrix component arith (spirv.FMul) is f16/f32/f64-only; a bf16 prologue elementwise feeding a matmul input (SwiGLU gate->w2, or A*A) infers COp (its user is the promoted-tile transfer_write, not the contract) -> absorbed into an illegal spirv.FMul on coopmatrix<...xbf16,MatrixAcc> -> metal-spirv legalization CRASH (exit1). Fix (default-on, opt-out NLEARN_COOP_ALLOW_BF16_ELEMENTWISE): exclude bf16 elementwise from coop absorption so it stays a REGULAR in-kernel vector op on the tile; matmul still coop-loads. VALIDATED: (a) repro compiles exit1->exit0; (b) REGRESSION-FREE — plain bf16 matmul still fully coop (4 simdgroup_matrix/64 mma, byte-identical), and gpt2-small/gpt2/vit/distilbert GNORM BIT-EXACT vs known-good (3.184227e5/3.202741e5/3.822555e5/3.103745e5). BOUNDARY (honest): keeping the fused bf16 prologue ON COOP needs input promoted-to-smem w/ a FITTING tile — repros go scalar (small/unpromoted, coop dropped) OR smem-overflow (FFN-sized 2048x768x3072 = 393KB > 32KB, full-K promotion). That's deep multi-turn tile tuning w/ UNCERTAIN payoff (dispatch-count reduction falsified as speed lever cont121); standard bench models are GELU/non-gated so don't even exercise the SwiGLU prologue. NOT spinning on speculative smem tuning. Fix is a robustness/generality win (bf16 prologue compiles), not yet a perf win. Deployed dylib FROZEN; standalone-only; hero not running. NEXT options (uncertain-EV, pick per steer): (i) measure SwiGLU-gate materialization cost on a llama-style bench (is prologue fusion even worth pursuing?) before smem-tile tuning; (ii) attempt smem-fit tile config for prologue-fused coop matmul; (iii) accept in-scope levers exhausted, surface scope decision.

