2026-07-16 cont313: ✅ LANDED a real native-matmul optimization (opt-in, correctness-gated). Found the Apple coop-matmul default seeds (4,4,PD0) — literally "copied from NVIDIA, not Apple-tuned" — are suboptimal for large 2D matmuls. (8,2,PD1) [8 subgroups / 2 MN-tiles / pipeline-depth 1] fits smem AND parallelizes wide-N: sweep-validated same-run on isolated matmuls: [8192x768x3072] 2.32->3.22 (+39%), [4096x768x3072] 2.85->3.12 (+9%), deep-K +3%, all BIT-IDENTICAL GNORM (config-only). Implemented shape-aware heuristic in AppleConfig.cpp setAppleMatmulConfig: rank-2 output + M>=2048 + N>=512 + both mult-16 -> (8,2,PD1); else default. Kept OPT-IN (NLEARN_COOP_APPLE_TUNE) NOT default because ViT's padded/odd-seq projections (M=B*592) still regress with (8,2) even after rank-2+mult-16+M>=2048 guards (vit 0.92->0.64), and standard bench configs (M<2048/bs2) see no gain. VALIDATED: DEFAULT (flag off) = baseline bit-identical + ZERO regression (gpt2 1.84, vit 0.92, distilbert 2.34); OPT-IN = large-M win (matmul 3.1-3.3). Net: real correctness-neutral win for LARGE-BATCH ALIGNED general-backend matmuls (M>=2048), safely gated. Doesn't help the hero (custom gemm) or standard small-M bench. First genuine perf lever this session (flash neutral, prologue robustness-only, fusion walled). NEXT: either (a) find a cleaner ViT-shape discriminator to make it default-on, or (b) the win is niche (large-M only) so hold as opt-in; the model-level gap remains fusion-walled (cont312). Deployed dylib FROZEN; standalone only; hero not running.

2026-07-16 cont314: ✅✅ DEFAULT-ON native-matmul win LANDED (the mult-32 discriminator cracked it). Root of the ViT regression: (8,2) with 8 subgroups needs every matmul dim MULT-32; ViT M=B*577 pads to 4624=16*289 (mult-16 NOT mult-32) and its backward K=4624 -> partial tile -> REGRESSES -31..-78%. Benefiting shapes (4096/8192/4736=128*37, gpt2/bert M=B*512, N=3072, K=768) are ALL mult-32. So the discriminator is MULT-32, not mult-16. Updated AppleConfig heuristic: rank-2 out, M>=2048, N>=512, AND every dim of out + BOTH inputs (covers K) %32==0 -> (8,2,PD1); else (4,4,PD0). Flipped to DEFAULT-ON (opt-out NLEARN_COOP_NO_APPLE_TUNE). VALIDATED (interleaved same-build A/B, bit-identical GNORM on all): gpt2 +2.5% (1.87 vs 1.82), bert +1.5-3.5% (2.04 vs 1.97), distilbert +3.4% (2.40 vs 2.32), gpt2-small +1.6% — and ViT SAFE 0.90=0.90 (excluded by mult-32) — plus up to +39% (M=8192) / +54% ([4736x768x768]) on large aligned matmuls. Correctness bit-identical everywhere (config-only change). This is a genuine, deployable, general-backend improvement (the directive's literal "native Apple matmul use the matrix units" — now better-tuned + default-on). DEPLOY CANDIDATE (low risk: bit-identical, opt-out available), awaiting Nik OK. Standalone build only; deployed dylib FROZEN; hero not running (hero uses custom gemm so unaffected). NEXT: surface as deploy candidate; the model-level 2x-to-jm gap beyond this remains fusion-walled (cont312).

2026-07-16 cont315: Reduction config tuning = DEAD END (confirms fusion, not config, is the reduction gap). Added env hooks NLEARN_RED_PT (parallelThreshold, def 256) + NLEARN_RED_VC (targetVectorCount, def 8) to setReductionConfig; swept 8 configs on the layernorm/softmax/bias f+b microbench. ALL cluster within +-5% (layernorm 3859-4051us vs MPS 2553; softmax 3054-3178 vs MPS 2405; bias 1309-1970) — best layernorm 128/8=3859 (-5% marginal), no config dominates across ops. So the 1.5-1.75x reduction gap vs MPS is NOT the occupancy/vector config (unlike matmul which had a real +2-39% config win) — it's the FUSION dispatch-explosion (MPS fuses LN into ~2 kernels, IREE emits 15), the walled lever (cont312). Hooks left in (default-neutral, harmless, future-probing). NET kernel-tuning conclusion: matmul config WAS the one tractable kernel lever (cont314 win: +2-3% models / up to +39% large, default-on deploy candidate); reductions are fusion-bound; transposes fine; fusion walled. SESSION DELIVERABLES (validated, standalone): (1) default-on mult-32 Apple matmul tuning [DEPLOY CANDIDATE], (2) bf16-prologue-fusion compile fix (makes aggressive-fusion correct + fixes crash), (3) full 2x-gap attribution + 2 memory corrections, (4) compiler-native flash (correct, neutral, gated). Deployed dylib FROZEN; hero untouched. NEXT: the matmul tune is the ready deployable win; remaining model gap = walled fusion (deep/multi-week) or out-of-scope hero kernels — needs a direction call.

2026-07-16 cont316: EXHAUSTIVELY VERIFIED "native matmul on matrix units" — optimally met. Pipeline census (naive2l causal): 2D matmul coop=14/14, attention batch_matmul coop=0/3 (q@kT 512x512x64, a@v 512x64x512, bwd 64x512x512 all SCALAR). Confirmed via NLEARN_COOP_DEBUG the attention BMMs reach setCooperativeMatrixConfig and deduceMMASchedule REJECTS them; NLEARN_COOP_ALLOW_TRANSPOSE_EPILOGUE doesn't change it (not the epilogue check), and a@v [512x64x512] stays SCALAR under ALL seed configs (SG/MNT 4/4..1/1) — batched + N=64 small output => no valid schedule, not tunable. q@kT coop already FALSIFIED (K=64 too small, memory cont80-88). a@v (K=512 large) was the one un-falsified candidate but is unschedulable via config + memory says "do NOT re-attempt batch-matmul promotion" + N=64 uncertain-EV => dead. So the directive's goal is OPTIMALLY MET: large FFN/proj matmuls = coop + Apple-tuned (cont314 win); attention BMMs = correctly scalar (coop can't help/schedule). IN-SCOPE KERNEL SPACE NOW FULLY VERIFIED: matmul tune=WIN(deploy candidate), reductions=fusion-bound, attention-coop=dead, transposes=fine, fusion=walled. No un-checked in-scope kernel lever remains. Session deployable deliverable = the default-on mult-32 matmul tune (+2-3% models, up to +39% large, bit-identical). Deployed dylib FROZEN; hero untouched. NEXT: matmul tune ready for deploy call; model gap beyond = walled fusion (deep) / out-of-scope hero kernels.

2026-07-16 cont317: ⚠️ HONEST QUANTIFICATION of the matmul tune — real on isolated matmuls (+39%) but MARGINAL at model level (0-3%, structure-dependent), because the MODEL IS MEMORY/GLUE-BOUND not matmul-compute-bound. Naive L=12 BS=8 (M=4096, tune fires on ALL matmuls) interleaved: tune-ON 2.03/2.02 vs OFF 1.99/2.03 = NEUTRAL (noise), gnorm bit-identical. Contrast: cont314 FFN-heavy gpt2/bert showed +2-3% (real, matmul is a bigger fraction there); glue/attention-heavy naive shows ~0. So the matmul tune = correctness-neutral, +0-3% model (larger for FFN-heavy, ~0 for memory-bound), isolated +39% is compute-bound & NOT model-representative. RECONTEXTUALIZES THE CAMPAIGN: making native matmul use matrix units (P1+coop+my tune, all DONE) does NOT close the model-level gap because matmul COMPUTE was never the model bottleneck — the model is bound by the GLUE/FUSION memory traffic (reductions/transposes/elementwise that MPS fuses & IREE doesn't). This is the SAME fusion wall, now shown to be THE model-level bottleneck (matmul compute is not). Definitive: the directive's "native matmul on matrix units" is DONE and correct, but it's not the lever that closes the 2x gap — memory-bound glue-fusion is (walled, deep). Matmul tune still worth keeping (correctness-neutral, +2-3% FFN-heavy) but honestly marginal. Deployed dylib FROZEN; hero untouched. NEXT: the model-level gap is definitively fusion/memory-bound (not compute) — only the deep fused-kernel-codegen (register-resident intermediates, MPS-style) or out-of-scope custom kernels can close it; no in-scope compute-tuning lever will.

2026-07-16 cont318: TESTED THE LAST REGIME (long-seq) — walled too; in-scope space now EXHAUSTIVELY verified across ALL regimes. Compiler-native flash at T=4096 L=2 B=1 (scores=400MB/layer, the hero's seq): flash OFF 0.82 vs ON 0.82 = NEUTRAL, gnorm bit-identical — because flash DID NOT FIRE (0 [bwd-trace]; matcher gap: the causal-mask/softmax pattern at large T differs from T=512 where it fired 12/12). So long-seq general-backend attention materializes as SCALAR T^2 batch-matmuls (cont316: attention BMMs are scalar) = the T=4096 bottleneck (compute-bound on scalar attention, NOT memory-materialization). Coop attention is falsified (K=64/N=64 unschedulable, cont316); flash matcher-gap is niche (the HERO already uses custom flash_attention.metal, unaffected). COMPLETE REGIME MAP: short-seq = memory/glue-fusion-bound (walled); long-seq = scalar-attention-compute-bound (coop-falsified) + flash-matcher-gap (niche); matmul(FFN) = coop+tuned but NOT the bottleneck (cont317 memory-bound proof). EVERY in-scope lever across EVERY regime is now walled/falsified/niche/done. TERMINAL STATE (exhaustively verified, not asserted): directive's "native matmul on matrix units" = DONE+correct but proven NOT the gap-closing lever; the 2x gap is memory-bound glue-fusion (short) / scalar-attention (long), both requiring DEEP (register-resident fused codegen / attention kernel) or OUT-OF-SCOPE (hero custom kernels) work. Session deliverable = mult-32 matmul tune (correctness-neutral, +2-3% FFN-heavy, marginal). Deployed dylib FROZEN; hero untouched. NEXT: HARD BLOCKER — no incremental in-scope lever remains in any regime; needs a direction/scope call (deep fusion codegen vs hero kernels vs accept). Further in-scope compute probing = spinning.

2026-07-16 cont319: Confirmed the fusion -18% has NO bounded fix — it's fused-kernel codegen quality (deep). Aggressive-fusion dispatch list: matmul shapes IDENTICAL to unfused (1024x768x3072 etc.), coop coverage same; the delta is fused reduction/elementwise kernels (new: reduction_12288x512_bf16xf32, elementwise_1024x768_bf16xf32xbf16). So the slowdown is in how IREE tiles/schedules FUSED reduction+elementwise dispatches — not a flag/config/pipeline knob (all exhausted), but the register-resident-fusion codegen itself = deep multi-week. TERMINAL: no incremental in-scope lever remains anywhere (verified across matmul[win-but-not-bottleneck], reductions[fusion-bound], attention[scalar/falsified], flash[neutral+matcher-gap], fusion[correct-but-deep-codegen], all regimes short+long). ACTIONABLE DECISION (for Nik): (1) DEPLOY the mult-32 matmul tune — validated, correctness-neutral, +2-3% FFN-heavy, ready (backup+rollback trivial); (2) invest in DEEP fused-kernel codegen (the ~1.4% fusion win per mlx-benchmark ITEM4, multi-week, uncertain — needs register-resident reduction+elementwise fusion so fused kernels stop round-tripping memory); (3) pursue HERO custom kernels (mlx-benchmark ITEM3 cast-fold / RMSNorm fused kernel — out of strict iree-compile scope but the real MFU-north-star path since the hero uses custom kernels). Deployed dylib FROZEN; hero untouched. NEXT: hold validated standalone build; the campaign needs a direction call — no autonomous incremental in-scope step remains without spinning on proven-walled levers.

2026-07-16 cont320: DEFINITIVE proof — the 2x gap is AGGREGATE glue, no single-op lever closes it. Single-pass layernorm (share mean/var reduction): isolated f+b 4271->3220us = -25% (1.33x, IREE does NOT auto-fuse the 2 reductions), loss-correct. BUT model-level naive L=12 BS=8: two-pass 1.99/2.03 vs single-pass 2.06/2.02 = NEUTRAL — SAME wash-out as the matmul tune (cont317). This CONFIRMS from a 3rd independent angle: NO single-op fix (matmul +39% iso / layernorm +33% iso / reductions / flash) moves the model, because the model gap is the SUM of many small glue ops (each ~few% of the model), none dominant. Only WHOLE-GRAPH register-resident fusion (MPS-style, all glue fused into matmuls at once, no intermediate memory round-trips) closes the 2x = deep multi-week codegen (the ONLY remaining lever, confirmed). EXHAUSTIVELY PROVEN TERMINAL STATE: matmul(coop+tuned,not-bottleneck), reductions(fusion-bound), attention(scalar/falsified), flash(neutral+matcher-gap), fusion-flag(correct but -18% deep), single-op-glue(all marginal) — every in-scope incremental lever gives isolated-win/model-neutral. The 2x needs whole-graph fusion (deep) or out-of-scope hero kernels. HOLDING: further single-op probing re-confirms this (=spinning); no autonomous incremental in-scope step remains. Session deliverables banked (matmul tune deploy-candidate, bf16-prologue fix, full gap diagnosis). Deployed dylib FROZEN; hero untouched. Direction call needed: deploy matmul tune / commit to deep whole-graph fusion / pursue hero custom kernels.

