2026-07-16 cont322: DEEP-WORK STARTED — first mechanistic lead into the fusion -18%. Extracted the fused kernel MSL (aggressive-fusion, naive2l): main_dispatch_11_reduction_12288x512_bf16xf32 makes 58 CONSTANT-INDEX writes to threadgroup memory (_workgroup_mem_N._m0[i]=i, an iota/index array 0..57) + a threadgroup_barrier — indices that should be computed inline from thread_id, not materialized to smem. Candidate inefficiency: extra threadgroup traffic + barrier per fused reduction. (12288=24*512=B*H*T, reducing over 512 = a fused attention/LN-grad reduction.) Couldn't confirm fusion-introduced this turn (unfused kernel name mismatch in naive2l). This is a REAL lead into why IREE's fused reduction kernels are slow (not spinning — new mechanistic finding, aligned with persistence-over-premature-exhaustion: multi-week deep work is in scope). NEXT (deep, concrete): (1) confirm the iota-to-smem is fusion-introduced (match the unfused reduction kernel by exact name, diff); (2) trace the iota to its linalg source (linalg.index? an iota op in the fused elementwise? SPIR-V loop-index materialization?); (3) if removable (compute inline), patch the codegen and measure aggressive-fusion model-level (-18% -> ?); gate on correctness. Deployed dylib FROZEN; standalone; hero untouched. Banked: matmul tune [deploy candidate] + bf16-prologue fix + gap diagnosis.

