2026-07-16 cont324: 🎯🎯 BREAKTHROUGH — aggressive-fusion is a REAL +7-8% MODEL-LEVEL win (non-marginal!), reopens the fusion lever, corrects the premature "walled" conclusion. My cont311/312 "-18%/walled" was measured ONLY on the CAUSAL naive model — the causal-MASK fusion is the slow case. NEW ablation (bs8, non-causal, OFF vs AGGR gnorm): ffn 7.1048e1==7.1076e1 CORRECT +7%; ffn_ln 3.2681e5==3.2733e5 CORRECT +7.5% (532->492ms); full(+attention) DIVERGES. So aggressive-fusion (a) is CORRECT for FFN+LN glue and (b) gives +7-8% MODEL-LEVEL (unlike the matmul tune which was isolated-only/model-marginal — this is the FIRST non-marginal lever because fusion reduces AGGREGATE glue passes = attacks the proven memory-bound bottleneck). Real non-causal models bert/roberta/distilbert: aggr +8% (2.04->2.20 etc) BUT GNORM 34x off — miscompile LOCALIZED to the ATTENTION (softmax) BACKWARD fusion (FFN+LN fuse correctly; only attention-bwd breaks). This is the memory-bound-glue lever I proved was needed (cont317/320), now shown TRACTABLE: fusion works, just the attention-bwd miscompiles. NEXT (high-EV): (1) localize the attention-bwd miscompile (softmax-grad? the a@v/q@k fused-bwd?) via a smaller repro; (2) EITHER fix it OR exclude the attention softmax-backward from aggressive-fusion (capture the +7% FFN+LN clean); (3) validate GNORM bit-close + measure. Causal-mask -18% is a separate sub-issue. Deployed dylib FROZEN; standalone; hero untouched. Banked: matmul tune + bf16-prologue fix.

2026-07-16 cont324b: Miscompile localization refined — single-attention fwd+bwd does NOT reproduce the 34x (softmax gnorm 1.53->1.57, no-softmax 8.65->8.62, both ~correct); so the bert 34x is STRUCTURE-DEPENDENT (multi-layer residual+LN+attention interaction OR the embedding-lookup/scatter gradient which bert has and my simplified models don't). VALIDATED CORE (the real, usable finding): aggressive-fusion on FFN+LN = +7.5% CORRECT (ffn_ln gnorm bit-close 3.2681e5==3.2733e5, 532->492ms) — a NON-MARGINAL model-level fusion win on correct compute. bert's +8% is on WRONG compute (34x gnorm) so not trustable until the miscompile is fixed. So the lever = capture the +7% FFN+LN fusion on real models by EITHER fixing the structure-dependent attention/embedding-bwd miscompile OR selectively fusing (FFN+LN only, exclude attention/embedding-grad). NEXT: (1) determine if the 34x is embedding-grad (scatter) vs attention — add embedding-lookup to the repro; (2) if a specific fused op miscompiles, find the fusion-formation guard to exclude it (keep FFN+LN fusion). This is the first non-marginal lever (attacks the proven memory-bound glue) — worth the deep dig. Deployed dylib FROZEN; standalone; hero untouched.

2026-07-16 cont325: Miscompile PINNED to attention-bwd fusion (compounding); embedding ruled out. emb+ffn+ln (w/ embedding lookup+scatter grad, NO attn) aggressive-fusion CORRECT (1.3468e5==1.3480e5); emb+full (w/ attn) ~5% off at L=4 -> compounds to 34x at bert L=12. So the attention-backward fusion has a subtle systematic error that amplifies through deep backprop. STRATEGY (universal win): EXCLUDE attention (softmax + attention batch-matmuls) from aggressive-fusion -> captures the validated +7% FFN+LN fusion on ALL models AND avoids BOTH the non-causal miscompile AND the causal-mask -18% (both are attention-fusion problems). FFN+LN fusion is +7% CORRECT (cont324 ffn_ln validated). This = the first non-marginal, deployable, general fusion win (attacks the proven memory-bound glue). NEXT: find the DispatchCreation/FormDispatchRegions aggressive-fusion decision point; add a guard that keeps softmax/attention-batch-matmul ops OUT of aggressive fused regions (leave them on the default path); validate GNORM bit-close + measure +7% on real models. Deployed dylib FROZEN; standalone; hero untouched. Banked: matmul tune + bf16-prologue fix.

2026-07-16 cont326: Deep-work on the +7% fusion lever — miscompile localized further, 2 fix-sites ruled out. Embedding ruled out (emb+ffn+ln correct). Tried 2 FormDispatchRegions::isFusableWithConsumer guards (NLEARN_AGGR_BUFCHECK re-apply stack-alloc check; NLEARN_AGGR_RANK2ONLY exclude rank>=4) — BOTH no-effect (bert gnorm identically 1.120838e7 wrong). So the attention-bwd miscompile is NOT formed at the consumer-fusion decision. Found aggressiveFusion is MULTI-SITE in FormDispatchRegions: consumer-fusion (609, guarded, wrong site) + cloneableOptions.aggressive producer-cloning (481/794/838) + producer path (655/818); ElementwiseOpFusion pass (Passes.cpp:221) uses FIXED opts (not aggressive-gated). So the miscompiling attention-bwd fusion is likely the AGGRESSIVE PRODUCER-CLONING (cloneableOptions.aggressive=true clones the softmax-bwd reduction into the batch-matmul dispatch -> undersized-buffer/wrong-reduction). VALIDATED CORE STILL STANDS: aggressive-fusion +7% CORRECT on FFN+LN (cont324); this is the first non-marginal lever. NEXT: IR-diff a small attention fwd+bwd WITH vs WITHOUT aggressive (--compile-to=dispatch-creation, --mlir-print-ir-after each pass) to find the EXACT bad fused op; then guard THAT site (producer-cloning of softmax-bwd reductions) — keep FFN+LN. Guards left env-gated (inert default). Deployed dylib FROZEN; standalone; hero untouched. Banked: matmul tune + bf16-prologue fix.

2026-07-16 cont327: HONEST RECONCILIATION — the +7-8% aggressive-fusion is FORWARD-CORRECT (inference) but training-backward is the KNOWN deep bufferization bug. bert aggressive-fusion: LOSS 3.145730e6==3.144922e6 (0.026%, CORRECT forward) but GNORM 1.120838e7 vs 3.323142e5 (34x WRONG backward). So aggressive-fusion = +7-8% CORRECT for INFERENCE, miscompiles TRAINING backward — EXACTLY cont86-88's documented conclusion ("aggressive fusion +3-5% inference-only, unsafe for training, deep undersized-buffer bufferization bug"). My "breakthrough" (cont324) partially rediscovered the known inference-only fusion. Tried 4 FormDispatchRegions guards (consumer-bufcheck, rank2only, no-aggr-clone, iterspace) — ALL no-effect (gnorm stays 34x wrong) => the training-backward miscompile is NOT in fusion-formation, it's in the fused-kernel BUFFERIZATION CODEGEN (deep, matches the known bug). NUANCE I ADDED (real): my cont304 bf16 fix made the CAUSAL training-backward CORRECT (cont311, gnorm matches, but -18% causal-mask-slow); only the NON-CAUSAL training-backward still hits this bufferization bug; and the FFN+LN training fusion is CORRECT (only attention-bwd breaks). So a SELECTIVE FFN+LN-only training fusion WOULD be a correct win, but excluding attention needs a working guard (4 failed = the exclusion must be at the bufferization/codegen level, not fusion formation). NET: aggressive-fusion training win is blocked by the known deep bufferization bug; 4 formation-guards can't fix it; this is negative-EV per cont86-88 unless the deep bufferization bug is fixed (multi-week). Inference +7-8% is real but not the training MFU target. NEXT (if pursued): the fix is in the bufferization pass (undersized buffer for the fused attention-backward reduction), OR accept the known wall. Guards left env-gated (inert). Deployed dylib FROZEN; standalone; hero untouched. Banked: matmul tune + bf16-prologue fix (+ bf16 fix already made causal-training-fusion correct).

