2026-07-16 cont329: 🎯 ROOT-CAUSED the training-fusion miscompile via Metal GPU Validation (concrete, tractable — NOT vague bufferization). Ran aggressive-fused bert under MTL_DEBUG_LAYER=1 MTL_SHADER_VALIDATION=1: FIRST failure = `main_dispatch_4/6_matmul_4096x768x768: total used threadgroupMemoryLength(38912 w/ tune, 54272 no-tune) must be <= 32768`. So aggressive-fusion fuses epilogues into the BACKWARD dW/dX matmuls (4096x768x768), pushing their threadgroup memory to 38-54KB >> Apple's 32768 limit -> Metal mis-executes -> corrupted gradient (34x GNORM); FORWARD correct because only the backward matmul overflows. This is EXACTLY cont258's "undersized-buffer" bug, now PRECISE: SMEM OVERFLOW on fused backward matmuls. Independent of my matmul tune (tune 38912 < no-tune 54272, both over — my tune REDUCES it). Explains why 4 fusion-formation guards failed (the bug is the config/promotion smem budget, not the fuse decision) AND why forward is correct (fwd matmuls fit). FIX DIRECTION (bounded): enforce the smem budget for FUSED matmuls — at config/promotion time, if a matmul's fused epilogue+tiles exceed getMaxWorkgroupMemoryBytes (32768), reduce tile OR reject coop (fall to scalar/separate dispatch, correct) — keeps the FFN+LN fusions that FIT (+7%). NEXT: find where the fused-matmul smem is computed (SPIRVTileAndPromote / setCooperativeMatrixConfig sharedMemoryLimitInBytes=32768 is set but fusion adds smem after) and add the budget guard; validate GNORM correct + measure. This REOPENS the +7% training-fusion win with a concrete fix. Deployed dylib FROZEN; standalone (clean + matmul tune + bf16 fix); hero untouched.

