2026-07-22 cont437: TWO critical design insights for the variance-rewrite (both non-obvious, nearly got wrong): (1) MUST be LINALG-level, not StableHLO — at stablehlo sum(x^2)=reduce_add(multiply(x,x)) reads precomputed x^2 (operand-0=x^2) so it WON'T share operand-0 with sum(x) => no fusion; at linalg a generic reduction reads x directly + squares per-element in the body (operand-0=x) = the two_red.mlir form that DID fuse. (2) rewrite = retarget the var-sum generic (reads center=x-mean, body mulf(c,c)+addf) to read x with body mulf(x,x)+addf = sum(x^2), then fix consumer: var=sum(x^2)/N - mean^2 (equivalently replace generic result with result - N*mean^2). Place the pattern BEFORE FuseHorizontalContractions so the two sum(x)/sum(x^2) generics then horizontally fuse. FULLY de-risked (numerics rel-err 0.0, fwd LN 4->2 dispatches) + FULLY specified (linalg pattern + exact correction). Bounded env-gated pass = clean next-session build.
